<title>UK: Sears shares active in &quot;b&amp;b&quot; tax trade.</title>
<headline>Sears shares active in &quot;b&amp;b&quot; tax trade.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in British retailer Sears were among London's most-active stocks on Tuesday after a so-called bed-and-breakfast trade, traders said.</p>
<p>Sears shares, which have gained recently on speculation of a break-up bid, were down 1/2p at 94-1/2p by 1347 GMT. Just short of 15 million stocks had changed hands by that time, putting Sears second on the most-traded list.</p>
<p>In a bed-and-breakfast trade an investor parks a poorly-performing stock with a broker overnight to realise a loss for tax purposes.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
